WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.101 --> 00:00:10.662
The next afternoon Raoul visited Christine in her dressing room. She offered him tea and cookies, and asked him

2
00:00:10.663 --> 00:00:19.001
about his plans. Raoul was relieved that Christine was kind to him, although he was distressed that she was

3
00:00:19.002 --> 00:00:24.763
still wearing the gold ring. Raoul took her hand in his. "I wish you wouldn't wear this ring." "Why?"

4
00:00:24.764 --> 00:00:31.824
she asked. "Because I'd like to give you a wedding ring myself one day." "Hush!" Christine pulled her hand

5
00:00:31.825 --> 00:00:41.511
away. "You know there's no chance of that happening. Your brother would disapprove—" "I don't care what my brother

6
00:00:41.512 --> 00:00:53.095
thinks, but you obviously are still attached to this Angel of Music fellow!" Raoul said. "I don't understand the

7
00:00:53.096 --> 00:01:02.545
hold he has over you." Although Christine did not respond, her distress was obvious. She gathered up her things

8
00:01:02.853 --> 00:01:07.749
and announced she was going home. "Christine!" Raoul called after her, but she didn't turn back. The next morning

9
00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:13.129
he headed straight for Mama Valerius' apartment to see Christine. "Oh, she left last evening and said she would

10
00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:22.431
be gone for two days," Mama Valerius said, sitting up straight in bed. Raoul was shocked. "So, she won't

11
00:01:22.432 --> 00:01:30.869
be back until tomorrow when she's scheduled to sing?" "That's correct." Raoul asked more questions about Christine's whereabouts, but

12
00:01:31.089 --> 00:01:42.383
Mama Valerius obviously knew nothing. He would have to wait until the next evening to see Christine at the

13
00:01:42.384 --> 00:01:51.306
opera. Carlotta had not performed since the infamous night when she croaked like a frog and the chandelier plunged

14
00:01:51.307 --> 00:01:57.284
into the audience. She'd canceled her contract, and Christine was temporarily offered her roles. When Raoul went to the

15
00:01:57.285 --> 00:02:02.800
opera the next night, he sat in his brother's box as usual. At the end of the final act,

16
00:02:03.966 --> 00:02:09.266
Christine received a standing ovation. Suddenly Raoul heard a man's voice whispering in his ear. "She's wearing the ring

17
00:02:09.267 --> 00:02:25.041
tonight, a ring that's not from you. She gave her soul again tonight, and she didn't give it to

18
00:02:25.042 --> 00:02:36.453
you!" Startled, Raoul searched the box but found no one. "I was seeing and hearing things when Christine disappeared

19
00:02:36.454 --> 00:02:44.541
into the mirror," he thought, "and now I must be hearing things again." He ran backstage and waited for

20
00:02:44.542 --> 00:02:51.394
Christine to come offstage. "Hurry up! Come with me!" Christine dragged Raoul to her dressing room and shut the

21
00:02:51.395 --> 00:02:59.316
door. Raoul threw himself on his knees before her. "Christine, I cannot spend another hour without you. I don't

22
00:02:59.317 --> 00:03:07.963
care what my brother—or anyone else—thinks about a viscount marrying an opera singer. Please marry me." Christine cried. "Oh,

23
00:03:08.543 --> 00:03:14.032
yes!" The couple kissed, but Christine soon tore herself away. She seemed to be listening to something, and with

24
00:03:14.033 --> 00:03:25.419
a quick gesture, motioned for Raoul to leave. He frowned. "Leave, why? We should celebrate our engagement." At the

25
00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:31.788
door she said softly, "Until tomorrow, my dear betrothed! Be happy, Raoul, because I sang for you tonight!" Raoul

26
00:03:31.789 --> 00:03:42.037
nodded. Those words made up for her sending him away. *** The next afternoon the couple met again in

27
00:03:42.038 --> 00:03:47.074
Christine's dressing room. "Let's go for a walk, dear." Christine linked her arm through Raoul's. Raoul thought they would

28
00:03:47.075 --> 00:03:57.666
go outside, far away from the building where he constantly sensed Erik's presence. But Christine took him onstage and

29
00:03:57.667 --> 00:04:04.951
made him sit on a bench in the peaceful coolness of the first act's scene for that night's performance.

30
00:04:04.952 --> 00:04:13.856
Another day they wandered along the deserted paths of a garden whose flowers had been made in a backstage

31
00:04:14.383 --> 00:04:22.011
workshop. Then they cautiously walked along the catwalks high above the stage. It was as if the real world

32
00:04:22.012 --> 00:04:27.410
had been forbidden to Christine, and she were condemned to live in the artificial world of the theater. Like

33
00:04:27.411 --> 00:04:36.160
a benevolent queen, Christine took Raoul throughout her empire, which covered 17 floors, from ground to roof. Her subjects

34
00:04:36.342 --> 00:04:45.302
included seamstresses, carpenters, and cobblers. Raoul discovered that all of them loved her because she took an interest in

35
00:04:45.303 --> 00:04:56.922
their troubles and daily lives. And so the couple's time together sped by until one day when Christine became

36
00:04:56.923 --> 00:05:05.166
inexplicably nervous. That afternoon she started running through the opera house for no reason and just as suddenly stopped.

37
00:05:05.167 --> 00:05:12.658
"This way! This way!" Christine said with a breathless laugh as she dragged Raoul along. Her eyes were wild,

38
00:05:14.131 --> 00:05:27.175
and she seemed on the verge of tears. "Stop, Christine! What's wrong?" he asked. "What's made you so nervous?"

39
00:05:27.176 --> 00:05:33.790
"Nothing, I swear it's nothing." But Raoul was certain that something was upsetting her. Once, when they passed an

40
00:05:33.791 --> 00:05:41.125
open trapdoor, Raoul made her stop running and pointed at it. "You've shown me the upper part of the

41
00:05:41.126 --> 00:05:47.763
opera house, but there are strange stories of what goes on below the stage and in all the cellars.

42
00:05:47.764 --> 00:05:58.930
Shall we go down there?" "Never!" Christine clutched Raoul tightly, as if she feared he'd disappear into the black

43
00:05:58.931 --> 00:06:06.060
hole. "Besides, it's not my world. Everything underground belongs to him." "So Erik lives down there, does he?" "No,

44
00:06:06.061 --> 00:06:14.607
no, I never said that." Christine started to walk away. "Come along, Raoul! Come away from that trapdoor." Much

45
00:06:15.166 --> 00:06:24.171
to their surprise, the trapdoor slammed shut. "Perhaps he was there listening to us!" Raoul said as he embraced

46
00:06:24.172 --> 00:06:35.157
Christine protectively. Christine shrugged. "No, he's too busy working." "Oh, he's working, is he?" Raoul was surprised that she

47
00:06:35.158 --> 00:06:48.265
knew so much about Erik's schedule. "What's he working on?" "A big project. But that's good for us because

48
00:06:48.266 --> 00:07:00.130
when he's working, he doesn't take a break for days. He doesn't eat or drink or have time to

49
00:07:00.131 --> 00:07:09.167
amuse himself with trapdoors." Raoul was still holding Christine in his arms when she seemed to lose her nerve.

50
00:07:09.168 --> 00:07:18.046
"Suppose it was him?" she asked. "Are you afraid of him?" Raoul asked. "Of course not! Let's go!" Christine

51
00:07:19.190 --> 00:07:30.104
took off running again. Despite protesting that she wasn't afraid, Christine was careful to avoid the trapdoors, and her

52
00:07:30.105 --> 00:07:37.821
agitation only increased with each passing day. One afternoon she arrived late for their meeting with such a desperate

53
00:07:37.822 --> 00:07:44.319
look on her face that Raoul had to speak. "I will remove you from Erik's power, Christine. And you

54
00:07:44.320 --> 00:07:50.945
won't be haunted by him anymore!" "Hush!" Christine looked around fearfully. "Suppose he heard you?" She pulled Raoul along

55
00:07:50.946 --> 00:07:57.497
to a top floor of the theater, far away from any trapdoors. Then she leaned in, but before she

56
00:07:57.606 --> 00:08:02.948
could kiss him, she became alarmed again. "Higher! We must go higher!" Raoul had trouble following her because they

57
00:08:03.429 --> 00:08:13.809
were soon under the roof in a maze of rafters and beams. Although Christine kept stopping to look behind

58
00:08:13.810 --> 00:08:27.802
them, she failed to see a shadow that stopped when she stopped and started up again when she did.

